title Publish the seed — scrub-fix (REDS #70) then the public push
prompt Keaton: push the seed
think The seed force-push is the AHOY3 custody gate, irreversible and public — so before touching it I regenerated the projection fresh from this session's whole tree (the Aug-10 seed predated all of it) and ran the full safety sweep.
think sow_witness was GREEN / IDENT_CLEAN, and my independent content scan confirmed no real name, family surname, .sol identity, poem line, or withheld dir crossed. Yet the scan ALSO caught garbled scrub output the clean verdict cannot see.
think REDS #70: every LICENSE read "Copyright 2026 the maintainer the maintainer and contributors", and family names read "a co-founder the maintainer the maintainer" / "a family member the maintainer". Cause: the scrub's compound-name rules (Keaton Dunsford · Robert Sealy Livermore · Alexandra Livermore) sat AFTER their single-token surname rules, so Livermore/Sealy/Dunsford resolved first and the compound never fired — the file's own "longest-first" law, unmet. My real-name LICENSE change this session exposed the Keaton-Dunsford case.
think Fixed by hoisting the three family full-names above the token rules in tools/fixtures/sow_scrub.sed. Re-projected: LICENSE now "the maintainer and contributors", the Siya executor "a co-founder (the maintainer's mother)", every garble gone, every name fragment absent.
think Verified the seed's commit identity is safe: authored "Grain OS <grain-os@users.noreply.github.com>" (depersonalized, no real name in metadata) and unsigned by the seed's local config — signing would attach the maintainer's key to the anonymized template; the initial commit is unsigned by design. Local main == remote main, so publishing is a fast-forward, not even a force-push.
obs The lesson (kin to REDS 61): a depersonalization verdict proves no name leaked, never that the scrubbed prose still reads. Before any public push, scan the projection's actual content — copyright lines, doubled role-words — not only the GREEN verdict.
obs This commit records the scrub fix, the red, and the log in the private tree; the seed publish is the next act (its own repo, its own push to grain-os/grain).
file tools/fixtures/sow_scrub.sed hoist compound family names above token rules (longest-first), closing the garble
file work-in-progress/REDS.md book #70 — scrub name-doubling caught by pre-push content scan, fixed, published
recommend keep-going publish the clean seed to grain-os/grain (fast-forward, Grain OS author, unsigned per seed design), then confirm the public HEAD
